            <ArticleTitle>The &quot;buddy-in-jail&quot; technique-a novel method for increasing support during percutaneous coronary intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>564-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.22049</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The &quot;buddy-in-jail&quot; technique is a novel method for increasing support during percutaneous coronary intervention. We report two case-based examples of successful coronary stent delivery using the jailed buddy wire technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
